  "boxes": [
    {
      "type": "anchorbox",
      "title": "The Ultimate Problem Solver",
      "description": "He takes 'impossible' tasks (Durgam) and makes them manageable (Sugam). When students face overwhelming exams, massive projects, or complex challenges, remembering his laser-like focus and unmatched work ethic provides a blueprint for making the impossible solvable.",
      "motivating_text": "",
      "citation": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "gotchabox",
      "items": [
        "Aspirated Consonants (म्ह and न्ह): In words like तुम्हरे (Tumhare) and कीन्हा (Keenhaa), the `h` merges with `m` and `n` to form a single aspirated sound. In classical Awadhi meter, this does not make the preceding short vowel heavy. Therefore, तु (tu) in Tumhare remains exactly 1 beat!"
      ]
    }
  ]
